# Environments. BOTH spellings of each, and that is not redundant: a trailing
# slash matches a DIRECTORY and never a symlink standing at the same path, so
# `.venv/` alone lets `git add -A` take the `.venv -> ../fut traffic/.venv`
# link every worktree needs. That is exactly how model/models,
# model/validation/out and model/validation/role_data were committed as
# absolute-path symlinks twice (see model/validation/lint_truth.py check 8,
# which now refuses a tracked symlink outright).
.venv
.venv/
venv
venv/
env
env/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Tool state
.gstack/

# Runtime state written by the dev launcher: pids and tailed logs for the two
# processes. Ephemeral by definition, and a stale pid in git is worse than no
# pid because jobs.py's liveness check reads one.
/.run/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Pipeline outputs written at the repo root. Leading slash on purpose: these
# match ONLY the root copies, never a committed fixture with the same name.
# tracks.json is ~57 MB for one half-match and is reproducible from the video,
# so it must never enter git history - you cannot remove it later without
# rewriting every commit that follows.
/tracks.json
/tracks.json.tmp
/calibration.json
/web/match.json
/season.json

# Job store. jobs.py creates this on first run and writes UPLOADED USER
# VIDEO into data/jobs/<id>/. Committing that is a disclosure incident, not a
# repo-size problem. Ignored before it exists rather than after.
#
# `/data/*`, not `/data/`: the footage READMEs and two vendored fixtures live
# under data/ too, and git cannot re-include anything under an excluded
# DIRECTORY. Everything else in data/ stays ignored, jobs included.
/data/*

# Source footage never belongs in git.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv
*.avi
# ...except the 20-frame excerpt check.py detect runs on (1.4 MB, an h264 stream
# copy of 118575's first 20 frames - author decision 2026-09-28).
!model/validation/fixtures/detect/*.mp4

# Ground-truth caches, ~4.6 MB each, derived by `validate.py --cache` from raw
# SoccerTrack halves that are ~2.7 GB apiece. Ignore them EXCEPT the one fixture
# test_golden.py needs: without it that test hits its SKIP path and exits 0,
# reporting success while testing nothing on every fresh clone.
model/validation/soccertrack/*.gz
!model/validation/soccertrack/118575_1st.tracks.json.gz

# DELIBERATELY COMMITTED, do not add these:
#   golden.json          - 1.7 KB, and it is the entire regression contract
#   model/validation/*.md      - measured results behind the README's claims
#   model/validation/run_*/    - 24 KB of accuracy reports, i.e. the evidence
#   web/*.html           - the zero-build front end IS the source

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Footage and its derived artifacts. All of it is downloadable from the sources
# recorded in the READMEs, so it is a cache, not source. Excluded WHOLESALE
# rather than by extension: an earlier version of this file only listed video
# extensions and would have committed 54 MB of remap tables (25 MB), evidence
# PNGs (15 MB) and annotation CSVs. Keep the READMEs - the provenance and
# licence of every clip is the part that actually matters and cannot be
# re-derived.
!/data/footage/
/data/footage/*
!/data/footage/README.md
!/data/footage/soccertrack/
/data/footage/soccertrack/*
!/data/footage/soccertrack/README.md

# Scratch outputs. model/validation/run*/ is deliberately NOT here: those reports are
# ~24 KB and they are the evidence behind (and now the retraction of) the numbers
# in NOISE_TOLERANCE.md. Keeping them is what makes the retraction checkable.
/web/tracks_demo.json
/web/match_demo.json
/web/calibration_demo.json
/serve_selfcheck.bin
.serve_selfcheck.bin

# Claude Code worktrees and local session state — never committed.
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
# Project skills are shared tooling, not session state.
!.claude/skills/

# Third-party checkouts studied but not vendored into the package. The glob is
# `/data/vendor/*` rather than `/data/vendor/` so a directory can be excepted
# below: re-including a path under an excluded DIRECTORY is impossible in git.
!/data/vendor/
/data/vendor/*

# EXCEPTION, and the reason is the same one the sigils exist for: ssac26 IS
# vendored - 12 KB of BSD-3 code and the 245 KB fixture that
# model/validation/vision_eval.py's @M numbers are measured on. A measurement whose
# inputs are not in the repo cannot be re-run from a fresh checkout, and at this
# size there is no reason it should not be. data/vendor/ssac26/PROVENANCE.md records
# the upstream commit and every local edit.
!/data/vendor/ssac26/

# Same exception, same reason: SkillCorner's published body-pose SAMPLE (1.8 MB,
# MIT) is the fixture model/validation/bodypose_eval.py's @M numbers are measured on.
# The FULL matches are not here - they are a 97 MB LFS file per match and live
# at ~/Downloads/skillcorner-opendata, the same way ~/Downloads/st2 does.
!/data/vendor/skillcorner/

# A trailing slash matches a DIRECTORY, not a SYMLINK at the same path - and these
# three have been committed as absolute-path symlinks twice now by `git add -A` in a
# worktree where they were linked to a checkout elsewhere. role_data's target is the
# deleted DFL export, so the pointer outlived the data it names. Both forms, on purpose.
/model/models
# `/model/validation/out` used to stand here, and it excluded the DIRECTORY.
# Since 2026-09-20 nine small result files under it are cited evidence and must
# be tracked, and git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded - so this excludes the CONTENTS instead. `/*` still matches a symlink
# standing at a child path; what it no longer does is block descent.
#
# THE SYMLINK DEFENCE FOR THIS ONE PATH MOVED, it was not dropped, and it moved
# to two things that run rather than a pattern that has to be read correctly:
# model/validation/lint_truth.py check 8 refuses ANY tracked symlink from the
# index, and verify_claims.py's preflight refuses to run a single claim if
# model/validation/out is a symlink (api.py's self-check breaks on one anyway).
# A pattern cannot tell a symlink from a directory it must descend into; those
# two checks can, and they fail loudly.
/model/validation/out/*
/model/validation/role_data
# CoreML model bundles: 58 MB, rebuilt with model/engine/coreml_worker.py --export
/model/models/

# model/validation/tune.py --selfcheck writes its sweep here; generated, not source
/model/validation/tune_runs/

# Crops + downloaded dataset for model/validation/train_roles.py: 80 MB and 372 JPEGs,
# both rebuilt by `--fetch`. The source of truth is the CC BY 4.0 dataset it
# names, not a copy of it in git.
/model/validation/role_crops.npz
/model/validation/role_data/

# Benchmark and eval artefacts: 335 MB of tracks JSON, contact sheets and
# TrackEval staging. All regenerated by model/validation/st2_*.py.
#
# EXCEPT THE RESULT FILES A CITED TAG READS. Until 2026-09-20 those nine numbers
# were re-derived by their producer on every push, so the evidence was the
# COMMAND and the file was scratch. The conversions that day made the evidence
# the FILE - and a file under an ignored directory is evidence that exists on one
# machine's disk. 96 KB against a repo whose whole premise is that a number must
# be checkable is not a trade worth making.
#
# THE FORM MATTERS, twice over:
#  * `model/validation/out/` excluded the DIRECTORY, and git cannot re-include a
#    file whose parent directory is excluded. So the contents are excluded with
#    `/*` and each level re-included on the way down. `/*` also matches a symlink;
#    a bare `dir/` does not, which is how three symlinks were committed twice.
#  * the re-includes for directories keep their trailing slash ON PURPOSE. That
#    form matches a real directory and never a symlink, so if one of these ever
#    becomes a link into another checkout, the negation quietly stops applying
#    and nothing is committed - it fails closed rather than committing a link.
model/validation/out/*

# The four-arm ball result, 1.7 KB. A cited tag that reads a file nobody else has
# is not re-runnable (same rule as the nine stc2025 artefacts below).
!model/validation/out/ball/
model/validation/out/ball/*
!model/validation/out/ball/cmp.json

!model/validation/out/stc2025/
model/validation/out/stc2025/*
!model/validation/out/stc2025/n22_results.json
!model/validation/out/stc2025/n23_results.json
!model/validation/out/stc2025/n24_results.json
!model/validation/out/stc2025/n25_results.json
!model/validation/out/stc2025/n26_results.json
!model/validation/out/stc2025/n27_results.json

!model/validation/out/st2_events/
model/validation/out/st2_events/*
!model/validation/out/st2_events/G2-e150.json
!model/validation/out/st2_events/G2-e40.json
!model/validation/out/st2_events/G3.json

# Rendered evidence and overlays: large, regenerable from model/validation/ scripts
data/renders/

# Obsidian per-user UI state. The vault config in .obsidian/app.json IS
# committed (it carries the node_modules ignore filters, without which the
# graph indexes 1714 package READMEs); the pane layout and cache are not.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache

# A lane manifest exists only while several agents share this tree. It arms the
# ownership check in .githooks/pre-commit; committed, it would arm it forever.
/.lanes.json

# The scraped feed data. /data/* already covers the store, but data/jobs and
# data/bios were force-added onto this branch as a demo fixture, and an ignore
# rule does not untrack what is already in the index - they were removed from it
# explicitly. They are a third party's match reports and player profiles, held
# with no licence to redistribute them, so they stay out of git and out of the
# app bundle. Local copies under data/ are fine: that is development against a
# feed, not distribution of it.
#
# app/desktop/resources/demo-job is NOT ignored - that copy is synthetic, generated
# by model/engine/demo.py, and is ours to ship.
model/validation/ball_cands_*.json.gz
# ...except the three A/B arms N48 rules on: 888 KB total, and a @M that reads a
# cache nobody else has is not re-runnable (docs/experiments/n48-ball-detector-ab.md).
!model/validation/ball_cands_*.cmpA.json.gz
!model/validation/ball_cands_*.cmpB.json.gz
!model/validation/ball_cands_*.cmpC.json.gz
# ...and N52's clean arm D, 1.7 MB. Without these six the SUPPORTED verdict at
# D-C +0.3644 exists only in a commit message and on one machine, which is the
# failure this repo was built to refuse.
!model/validation/ball_cands_*.cmpD.json.gz
# ...and the 640-era caches, 5.1 MB, by the SAME argument as the comment above - which
# applied to them the moment N65 found every number above was measured at the RFDETRNano
# default of 384 instead of the 640 the checkpoint was trained at. docs/experiments/n65-every-ball-number-was-measured-at-384.md and docs/experiments/n67-fewer-candidates-does-not-help-the-picker.md's
# PUBLISHED numbers are read from these four and from nothing else, so gitignoring them left
# the current results on one machine while the withdrawn ones were committed.
!model/validation/ball_cands_*.cmpDr.json.gz
!model/validation/ball_cands_*.cmpE1r.json.gz
!model/validation/ball_cands_*.cmpD1P.json.gz
!model/validation/ball_cands_*.cmpE2.json.gz

# The two compatibility paths left by the root restructure: `models` is a symlink
# to model/models and `validation/` is a REAL directory of symlinked children
# (api.py --verify breaks if it is a symlink). Both are machine-local pointers and
# have been committed by accident twice; an absolute symlink in git is one
# machine's layout published as source. lint_truth check 8 refuses the tracked form.
/models
/validation/

# Not published: personal data, internal notes, third-party feeds
data/photos/
data/rosters/
data/org.json
data/vendor/skillcorner/
/docs/memory/
.claude/
.obsidian/
model/validation/claims.log
